-- The issue #7 Hello World: a no-LHS machine (§1 one-shot) runs once,
-- unconditionally, at program start, emits (Stop, 0), and the Stop
-- machine exits cleanly. The one-shot form is `:` at the start of a
-- line — an empty join pattern.
: [say "Hello world!"; (Stop, 0)]
(Stop, c) : if c then [say "Error, closing"; exit c] else [exit c]
